            <ArticleTitle>Gallbladder torsion presenting as chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>W25-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/147870810X12659688851357</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While acute torsion of the gallbladder is an uncommon pathology, as this case demonstrates, it can present with sudden onset of chest pain, and must be borne in mind as a differential diagnosis in this patient demographic if early recognition and definitive management are to be made possible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
